WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.313 --> 00:00:01.287
(dramatic music)

00:00:01.287 --> 00:00:03.475
- [Narrator] This is a Chinese alligator.

00:00:03.475 --> 00:00:06.355
Native to eastern China, it is so rare

00:00:06.355 --> 00:00:10.406
that there are only 130 left in the wild.

00:00:10.406 --> 00:00:12.577
Known as the Yangtze alligator,

00:00:12.577 --> 00:00:17.009
it is one of the smallest
crocodilians in the world.

00:00:17.009 --> 00:00:20.179
Their stocky body is covered
in hard scales on the back

00:00:20.179 --> 00:00:22.227
and its blunt teeth are perfect

00:00:22.227 --> 00:00:26.057
for crushing shelled animals,
like clams and snails.

00:00:26.057 --> 00:00:29.249
Their menu also includes fish, insects,

00:00:29.249 --> 00:00:32.539
birds, and the occasional small mammal.

00:00:32.539 --> 00:00:36.169
They stay in subtropical areas
with fresh water sources,

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:40.316
like lakes, ponds, marshes, and streams.

00:00:40.316 --> 00:00:43.438
Sadly, these habitats are disappearing,

00:00:43.438 --> 00:00:45.889
often to make room for agriculture.

00:00:45.889 --> 00:00:48.166
This and poaching are the biggest threats

00:00:48.166 --> 00:00:50.358
to the survival of the species.

00:00:50.358 --> 00:00:52.558
Luckily, they do well in captivity,

00:00:52.558 --> 00:00:54.459
as they have been successfully bred

00:00:54.459 --> 00:00:57.387
in wildlife refuges and zoos.

00:00:57.387 --> 00:00:59.887
This is the Chinese alligator.

